item.text:
Three arrangements were compared internally:

- rotating the entire display/Pi stack 180° so its crowded edge points down;
- leaving the stack coupled and using multiple panel extensions;
- decoupling the display from a Pi/NVMe cassette and giving the crowded display edge an internal rear cable gallery.

The third is selected. It preserves the landscape 40×13 UI, keeps native Pi USB/Ethernet directly reachable on the right, keeps high-current USB-C power direct rather than through a questionable extension, and turns the display’s unidentified connectors into short, protected internal links. The image-generation skill now causes the one permitted picture to be created: one polished presentation sheet of this single selected design, with no alternate concepts.
